               <msContents>
                  <summary>A translation into Spanish of pts. 2, 3, 4 and; 5 of Brown's Elementa medicinae first published in Edinburgh, 1780.  Produced in Mexico.  
                     Dated Mexico 2 March 1808, but unsigned.  Although José Mariano Mociño [1757-1820], a member of the Royal Botanical Expedition to New Spain, is known 
                     to have translated and adapted the Elementa, only Pt. I was published [see M.28]. The present MS is either an independent translation (Mociño left for Spain in 1803) 
                     or perhaps a fair copy of his draft. [See Rickett (1947) pp. 38, 74].</summary>
                  
                  <textLang mainLang="es">Spanish</textLang>
                  
